{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:08:54.557Z","id":"83032a70357e2973b633bd1f","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67%40bytedance.com/","channels":["linux-arch"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67%40bytedance.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:08:54.557Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v10 4/8] mm: add a template-based fast path for zone-device page init","messages":{"178688187038.2799959.7142225711373927632.b4-review@b4":{"id":"178688187038.2799959.7142225711373927632.b4-review@b4","messageId":"178688187038.2799959.7142225711373927632.b4-review@b4","references":["20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","20260810122057.30447-5-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260810122057.30447-5-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"],"author":{"name":"Mike Rapoport","address":"rppt@kernel.org"},"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T12:04:30.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T12:04:30.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v10 4/8] mm: add a template-based fast path for zone-device page init","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi,"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"memmap_init_zone_device() repeats nearly identical head-page"},{"depth":1,"text":"initialization for each PFN. Prepare one reusable ZONE_DEVICE head-page"},{"depth":1,"text":"template through the existing slow path, refresh the PFN-dependent"},{"depth":1,"text":"fields in that template before each copy, and memcpy it into each"},{"depth":1,"text":"destination page."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Use the template path unconditionally. The page_ref_set tracepoint is"},{"depth":1,"text":"primarily a debugging aid, while this code is still initializing struct"},{"depth":1,"text":"pages before they are handed out. From the perspective of users of those"},{"depth":1,"text":"pages, the initialization-time refcount transitions are not part of the"},{"depth":1,"text":"observable page lifetime."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This means page_ref_set will no longer observe every initialization-time"},{"depth":1,"text":"refcount assignment for copied ZONE_DEVICE head pages. The impact is"},{"depth":1,"text":"controlled because the final initialized struct page state is unchanged,"},{"depth":1,"text":"and keeping a separate non-template path only for this local tracepoint"},{"depth":1,"text":"observability would add complexity to the common path."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This patch accelerates head-page initialization. The pfns_per_compound"},{"depth":1,"text":"== 1 case gets the full benefit here, compound tails are handled in the"},{"depth":1,"text":"next patch."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Tested in a VM with a 100 GB fsdax namespace device configured with"},{"depth":1,"text":"map=dev on Intel Ice Lake server. This test exercises the nd_pmem rebind"},{"depth":1,"text":"path (pfns_per_compound == 1)."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Test procedure:"},{"depth":1,"text":"Rebind the nd_pmem driver 30 times and collect the memmap initialization"},{"depth":1,"text":"time from the pr_debug() output of memmap_init_zone_device()."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Base(v7.2-rc1):"},{"depth":1,"text":"  Average of rebinds for nd_pmem driver: 244.28 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"With this patch and its prerequisites applied:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  Average of rebinds for nd_pmem driver: 215.55 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This reduces the average memmap initialization time measured during rebind"},{"depth":1,"text":"from 244.28 ms to 215.55 ms, or about 11%."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Li Zhe <lizhe.67@bytedance.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/mm/mm_init.c b/mm/mm_init.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index a70acb7431a6..56a36a71ba89 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/mm/mm_init.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/mm/mm_init.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1065,6 +1065,35 @@ static void __ref zone_device_page_init_slow(struct page *page,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tset_page_count(page, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * 'template' is a reusable page prototype rather than a strictly immutable"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * object. Most ZONE_DEVICE fields stay constant across the pages covered by"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * the current template, but section bits and page->virtual may still depend"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * on the PFN. Refresh those PFN-dependent fields in the template before"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * copying it into @page."},{"depth":1,"text":"+ */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+static inline void zone_device_page_update_template(struct page *template,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tunsigned long pfn)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tset_page_section_from_pfn(template, pfn);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#ifdef WANT_PAGE_VIRTUAL"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (!is_highmem_idx(ZONE_DEVICE))"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tset_page_address(template, __va(pfn << PAGE_SHIFT));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#endif"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+static void zone_device_page_init_from_template(struct page *page,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tunsigned long pfn, struct page *template)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t * 'template' carries the invariant portion of a ZONE_DEVICE struct"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t * page. Update the PFN-dependent fields in place before copying it"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t * to the destination page."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tzone_device_page_update_template(template, pfn);"}],"lineCount":75,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Looks like it's the only user of zone_device_page_update_template().\nI'd just fold it here and drop the comment."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"+\tmemcpy(page, template, sizeof(*page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" /*"},{"depth":1,"text":"  * With compound page geometry and when struct pages are stored in ram most"},{"depth":1,"text":"  * tail pages are reused. Consequently, the amount of unique struct pages to"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1127,6 +1156,7 @@ void __ref memmap_init_zone_device(struct zone *zone,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned long zone_idx = zone_idx(zone);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned long start = jiffies;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tint nid = pgdat->node_id;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tstruct page template;"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" \tif (WARN_ON_ONCE(!pgmap || zone_idx != ZONE_DEVICE))"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\treturn;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1144,7 +1174,22 @@ void __ref memmap_init_zone_device(struct zone *zone,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tfor (pfn = start_pfn; pfn < end_pfn; pfn += pfns_per_compound) {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tstruct page *page = pfn_to_page(pfn);"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tzone_device_page_init_slow(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid, pgmap);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (pfn == start_pfn) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * Seed the reusable head-page template from the"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * first real struct page. This initializes the"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * first page through the existing slow path and"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * then reuses that final state as the template"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * for subsequent pages."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tzone_device_page_init_slow(page, pfn, zone_idx,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\t\t   nid, pgmap);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t/* init template page */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tmemcpy(&template, page, sizeof(*page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t} else {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tzone_device_page_init_from_template(page, pfn,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t    &template);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t}"}],"lineCount":35,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Why can't we init the template for the first page being initialized and\nthen call zone_device_page_init_from_template() unconditionally?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The same applies to the tail pages initialization."},{"kind":"signature","text":"Sincerely yours,\nMike.","lineCount":2}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260810122057.30447-5-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"},"178688187038.2799959.7900723270155108493.b4-review@b4":{"id":"178688187038.2799959.7900723270155108493.b4-review@b4","messageId":"178688187038.2799959.7900723270155108493.b4-review@b4","references":["20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","20260810122057.30447-3-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260810122057.30447-3-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"],"author":{"name":"Mike Rapoport","address":"rppt@kernel.org"},"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T12:04:30.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T12:04:30.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v10 2/8] mm: factor zone-device page init helpers out of __init_zone_device_page","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi,"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"memmap_init_zone_device() currently mixes refcount policy and core"},{"depth":1,"text":"ZONE_DEVICE page setup in a single helper."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Factor the refcount-reset predicate into pagemap_requires_refcount_reset(),"},{"depth":1,"text":"move the common page initialization into __zone_device_page_init(), and"},{"depth":1,"text":"wrap the existing slow path in zone_device_page_init_slow()."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This keeps the slow-path behaviour unchanged and gives later patches"},{"depth":1,"text":"reusable helper boundaries."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"No functional change intended."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Li Zhe <lizhe.67@bytedance.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Reviewed-by: Mike Rapoport (Microsoft) <rppt@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/mm/mm_init.c b/mm/mm_init.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 95808ab5cfdb..a70acb7431a6 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/mm/mm_init.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/mm/mm_init.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1005,11 +1005,37 @@ static void __init memmap_init(void)"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" #ifdef CONFIG_ZONE_DEVICE"},{"depth":1,"text":"-static void __ref __init_zone_device_page(struct page *page, unsigned long pfn,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * Return true when memmap_init_zone_device() must initialize the page"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * refcount to 0. MEMORY_DEVICE_GENERIC pages regain a refcount of 1 in"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * the free path, while the remaining ZONE_DEVICE types start from 0 here"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * and raise the count again when the allocator or driver hands the page"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * out."},{"depth":1,"text":"+ */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+static inline bool pagemap_requires_refcount_reset(const struct dev_pagemap *pgmap)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t * MEMORY_DEVICE_GENERIC pages regain a refcount of 1 in the free"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t * path. The remaining ZONE_DEVICE types start from 0 here and raise"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t * the count again when the allocator or driver hands the page out."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tswitch (pgmap->type) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_FS_DAX:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_PRIVATE:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_COHERENT:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_PCI_P2PDMA:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn true;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_GENERIC:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn false;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\treturn false;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+static void __ref __zone_device_page_init(struct page *page, unsigned long pfn,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t\t  unsigned long zone_idx, int nid,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t\t  struct dev_pagemap *pgmap)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t__init_single_page(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid);"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" \t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1028,23 +1054,15 @@ static void __ref __init_zone_device_page(struct page *page, unsigned long pfn,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t */"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tpage_folio(page)->pgmap = pgmap;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tpage->zone_device_data = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t * MEMORY_DEVICE_GENERIC pages regain a refcount of 1 in the free"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t * path. The remaining ZONE_DEVICE types start from 0 here and raise"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t * the count again when the allocator or driver hands the page out."},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tswitch (pgmap->type) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_FS_DAX:"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_PRIVATE:"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_COHERENT:"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_PCI_P2PDMA:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+static void __ref zone_device_page_init_slow(struct page *page,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tunsigned long pfn, unsigned long zone_idx, int nid,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tstruct dev_pagemap *pgmap)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t__zone_device_page_init(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid, pgmap);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (pagemap_requires_refcount_reset(pgmap))"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tset_page_count(page, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tbreak;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tcase MEMORY_DEVICE_GENERIC:"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tbreak;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" /*"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1090,7 +1108,7 @@ static void __ref memmap_init_compound(struct page *head,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tfor (pfn = head_pfn + 1; pfn < end_pfn; pfn++) {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tstruct page *page = pfn_to_page(pfn);"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t__init_zone_device_page(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid, pgmap);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tzone_device_page_init_slow(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid, pgmap);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tprep_compound_tail(page, head, order);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tset_page_count(page, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1126,7 +1144,7 @@ void __ref memmap_init_zone_device(struct zone *zone,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tfor (pfn = start_pfn; pfn < end_pfn; pfn += pfns_per_compound) {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tstruct page *page = pfn_to_page(pfn);"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t__init_zone_device_page(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid, pgmap);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tzone_device_page_init_slow(page, pfn, zone_idx, nid, pgmap);"}],"lineCount":105,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"It looks like all callers of __init_zone_device_page() are now calling\nzone_device_page_init_slow() that with series evolution became a thin\nwrapper for __zone_device_page_init()."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Maybe we can just rename __init_zone_device_page() to\n__zone_device_page_init() and replace the open coded setting of the page\ncount with the call to pagemap_requires_refcount_reset() an be done\nhere?"},{"kind":"signature","text":"Sincerely yours,\nMike.","lineCount":2}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260810122057.30447-3-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"},"178688187038.2799959.10744801601222444417.b4-review@b4":{"id":"178688187038.2799959.10744801601222444417.b4-review@b4","messageId":"178688187038.2799959.10744801601222444417.b4-review@b4","references":["20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","20260810122057.30447-2-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260810122057.30447-2-lizhe.67@bytedance.com","20260810122057.30447-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"],"author":{"name":"Mike Rapoport","address":"rppt@kernel.org"},"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T12:04:30.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T12:04:30.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v10 1/8] mm: fix stale ZONE_DEVICE refcount comment","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arch.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Mon, 10 Aug 2026 20:20:50 +0800, Li Zhe <lizhe.67@bytedance.com> wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The comment in __init_zone_device_page() still uses the old"},{"depth":1,"text":"MEMORY_TYPE_* names and implies that FS_DAX pages regain a"},{"depth":1,"text":"refcount of 1 in the free path. That no longer matches the code."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Update the comment to describe the current policy correctly:"},{"depth":1,"text":"MEMORY_DEVICE_GENERIC pages regain a refcount of 1 in the free path,"},{"depth":1,"text":"while the remaining ZONE_DEVICE types start from 0 here and raise the"},{"depth":1,"text":"count again when the allocator or driver hands the page out."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"[...]"}],"lineCount":10,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Reviewed-by: Mike Rapoport (Microsoft) <rppt@kernel.org>"},{"kind":"signature","text":"Sincerely yours,\nMike.","lineCount":2}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260810122057.30447-2-lizhe.67@bytedance.com"}},"rootIds":["178688187038.2799959.7142225711373927632.b4-review@b4","178688187038.2799959.7900723270155108493.b4-review@b4","178688187038.2799959.10744801601222444417.b4-review@b4"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["178688187038.2799959.7142225711373927632.b4-review@b4","178688187038.2799959.7900723270155108493.b4-review@b4","178688187038.2799959.10744801601222444417.b4-review@b4"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}